title: '[EPMB] Add configurable reward source and slash destination to signed phase'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `type RewardSource` (pay rewards from a pot account instead of minting) and `type Slash`
    (route slashed deposits to a handler instead of burning) to
    `pallet-election-provider-multi-block::signed::Config`. Asset Hub and the staking-async
    parachain runtime now wire both through the DAP buffer, keeping `TotalIssuance` reconcilable
    with the DAP emission curve.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    If a `RewardSource` pot is depleted, a round-winner's reward is no longer just logged as
    failed: it is queued and can be claimed by anyone via the new permissionless
    `claim_unpaid_reward(round)` call, free of charge on success, paying out to the original
    winner. The queue holds at most 16 entries; if full, the oldest is evicted to make room.
crates:
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-block
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: minor
